WEBVTT

00:48:27.973 --> 00:48:31.783
Some people will say that AI
has the ability itself to be creative,

00:48:31.807 --> 00:48:33.729
and I think there's a debate about that.

00:48:33.753 --> 00:48:36.483
But you would, I think,
argue that only to an extent,

00:48:36.507 --> 00:48:39.744
and that humans,
for the foreseeable future,

00:48:39.768 --> 00:48:43.918
maybe until we have superintelligence
in 60 or 100 or 500 years' time,

00:48:43.942 --> 00:48:45.164
are just more creative.

00:48:45.188 --> 00:48:47.220
That's something
that we're really good at,

00:48:47.244 --> 00:48:49.321
and we care about human
forms of creativity.

00:48:49.345 --> 00:48:50.678
So that is one axis.

00:48:51.131 --> 00:48:54.012
You know, creative jobs
versus less creative jobs.

00:48:54.036 --> 00:48:58.758
And the other axis is linked
to compassion or empathy or human values,

00:48:58.782 --> 00:49:02.707
which you describe
as social or asocial jobs.